<title>FRANCE: Reuters seventh ex-Paris air cargo market report.</title>
<headline>Reuters seventh ex-Paris air cargo market report.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Below are current average ex-Paris French franc air cargo rates per kilo for a 100 kg shipment with volume-to-weight ratio of six-to-on.</p>
<p>						  Sept 11	  July 5</p>
<p>				    NORTH AMERICA</p>
<p>    PAR-JFK				   5.45	     5.45</p>
<p>    PAR-CHI				   5.90	     5.95</p>
<p>    PAR- LA				   6.65	     6.65</p>
<p>    PAR-YUL				   6.70	     6.70</p>
<p>				    ASIA/PACIFIC</p>
<p>    PAR-SEL				  11.40	     11.40</p>
<p>    PAR-NAR				  14.70	     14.70</p>
<p>    PAR-TPE				   7.70		7.75</p>
<p>    PAR-HKG				   8.40		8.40</p>
<p>    PAR-SIN				   8.20		8.20</p>
<p>    PAR-NOU (New Caledonia)	    39.95	     39.95</p>
<p>    PAR-PPT  (Tahiti)		    33.35	     33.35</p>
<p>				    MIDDLE EAST</p>
<p>    PAR-DXB				   5.40		5.50</p>
<p>				    INDIAN OCEAN</p>
<p>    PAR-RUN (Reunion)		     21.15	    21.15</p>
<p>				    FRENCH WEST INDIES</p>
<p>    PAR/FDF/PTP			     14.70	     14.70</p>
<p>				    AFRICA</p>
<p>    PAR-JNB				   14.60	     14.80</p>
<p>The rates quoted in this report were obtained by Reuters on a confidential basis  from a range of airlines, large forwarders and smaller cargo agents based at the Paris airports.</p>
<p>	   All prices are quoted in French francs.</p>
<p>	  The tariffs represent average rates calculated from a</p>
<p>range of prices and are indicative of current market activity.</p>
</text>
